# Copy to .env and fill in as needed — the app works fully without any of
# these (see README, "runs without an API key"): with an empty .env, /answer
# returns comparable markets and statistics with no LLM-drafted text, which
# is the supported default, not a degraded fallback.

# Optional: enables LLM-drafted answers with citations, via any
# OpenAI-compatible chat completions endpoint. Example using Groq's free
# tier instead of OpenAI itself:
#   OPENAI_API_KEY=<your Groq key>
#   OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
#   OPENAI_MODEL=llama-3.1-8b-instant
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# Optional: local fallback used when no OPENAI_API_KEY is set and an
# Ollama server is reachable at this address.
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
# OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.2

# Optional: where downloaded/normalized data is stored.
# DECP_DATA_DIR=data
